  (text "TMS9118 VDP $C020: MODE = A0 (0 = VRAM data, 1 = registers/status).  /CSR and\n/CSW come from a 74HC138 enabled by VDP_SEL and PHI2 (stretched for I/O\ncycles), with A0 = R/W.  /INT goes to VIA CB1.  16K VRAM in two TMS4416s\n(16K x 4): address A0-A7 = AD7-AD0, data on RD0-RD3 and RD7-RD4, /G tied low.\nLeave time between VRAM accesses (up to several us in some modes).\nVideo: NTSC composite, 256x192, 15 colours, 32 sprites.  2N3904 emitter\nfollower into 75 ohm, to a small composite LCD monitor (most also take PAL).\nThe VRAM wiring and video buffer follow the PICerino TMS9118 board (MIT).\nRCA jack: Same Sky (CUI) RCJ-014, footprint in lib/MyParts.pretty." (at 25.4 246.7 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 0525ced6-e891-45d3-ab4b-accae9819454)
  )
)
